    "author_association": "NONE",
    "body": "### Problem\n\nMulticursor is very intelligent. If you:\n1. first place a bunch of cursors\n2. press `i`, and insert some text\nThen the cursors all update in real-time.\n\nHowever, this behavior seems to hook onto `i` in a way that's easy to break. If I set the rhs of `i` to something different, that still emits `i`:\n```lua\nvim.keymap.set(\"n\", \"i\", \"^i\")\n```\nThen other cursors are _not_ automatically updated, and only update when _leaving_ insert mode.\n\nThis is actually worse for `v_c`. Doing `viwc` with all cursors won't update in real-time if I set:\n```lua\nvim.keymap.set(\"x\", \"c\", '\"ac')\n```\nBut it _also_ won't work if another keymap emits `c`:\n```lua\nvim.keymap.set(\"x\", \"-\", \"c\")\n```\nAnd even doesn't work with:\n```lua\nvim.keymap.set(\"x\", \"c\", \"c\")\n```\n\n### Steps to reproduce\n\nFirst, create a file called `testing.txt` with these contents:\n```lua\nfirst line\nsecond line\n```\nTo demo neovim _without_ the problem, run `nvim --clean testing.txt`, then type `Qjitest`. You'll see that both cursors update in real-time, and insert `test` on both lines.\n\nNow, to demo the problem, add this line of code to `minimal.lua`:\n```lua\nvim.keymap.set(\"n\", \"i\", \"hi\")\n```\nNow run `nvim --clean -u minimal.lua testing.txt`, and type `Qjitest`. This time, the other cursor doesn't insert `test` until you type `<Esc>`.\nRepeat this for the other keymaps to test them as well. For the visual mode bindings, use `Qjviwctest`.\n\n### Expected behavior\n\nMulticursor would hook onto the action of `i` / `c` being emitted, and not care about how these mappings are emitted. I hit this with my personal mapping of `c` to `\"_c`, and I expect other people will have similar snippets that multicursor doesn't work with.\n\n### Nvim version (nvim -v)\n\nNVIM v0.13.0-dev Build type: Release LuaJIT 2.1.1785763465 Run \"nvim -V1 -v\" for more info\n\n### Vim (not Nvim) behaves the same?\n\nno, they have no multicursor\n\n### Operating system/version\n\nNixOS Unstable\n\n### Terminal name/version\n\nkitty 0.48.2\n\n### $TERM environment variable\n\nxterm-kitty\n\n### Installation\n\nnixpkgs",
